### 1. Fix Download Authorization in the Backend (VoucherQueryService.java)
The backend is currently blocking downloads because its security check only verifies if the user is the creator OR the *currently* pending role. Once a batch is rejected or moved past their step, it throws an "unauthorized" error.
We will update the authorization query to exactly match the viewing rules: If they created it, OR if their role is part of the workflow chain, they are allowed to download it.
**Find this method in VoucherQueryService.java:**
```java
    public boolean isUserAuthorizedForBatch(String batchId, String userId, Integer roleId) {
        Integer isCreator = jdbcTemplate.queryForObject("SELECT COUNT(*) FROM VOUCHER_POSTING WHERE BATCH_ID = ? AND CREATED_BY = ?", Integer.class, batchId, userId);
        if (isCreator != null && isCreator > 0) return true;
        Integer isAuthorized = jdbcTemplate.queryForObject("SELECT COUNT(*) FROM VOUCHER_POSTING vp JOIN WORKFLOW_TRANSITIONS wt ON vp.PENDING_AT = wt.WORKFLOW_ID WHERE vp.BATCH_ID = ? AND wt.ALLOWED_ROLE_ID = ?", Integer.class, batchId, roleId);
        return isAuthorized != null && isAuthorized > 0;
    }

```
**Replace it completely with this:**
```java
    public boolean isUserAuthorizedForBatch(String batchId, String userId, Integer roleId) {
        String sql = """
            SELECT COUNT(*) FROM VOUCHER_POSTING p 
            WHERE p.BATCH_ID = ? 
            AND (
                p.CREATED_BY = ? 
                OR EXISTS (
                    SELECT 1 FROM WORKFLOW_TRANSITIONS wt 
                    WHERE wt.WORKFLOW_CODE = p.WORKFLOW_CODE 
                    AND wt.ALLOWED_ROLE_ID = ?
                )
            )
        """;
        Integer isAuthorized = jdbcTemplate.queryForObject(sql, Integer.class, batchId, userId, roleId);
        return isAuthorized != null && isAuthorized > 0;
    }

```
